\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Why Alberto Fernandez's announcement of his debt negotiation plan didn't change the moodiness of the markets\b0\par\par\uc2 1,270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Foreign exchanges entered at the price of the dollar with liquidation - the highest value - to buy the MEP dollar, the one on the stock exchange which is $3 cheaperThe dollar was always contained by the sale of official banks. The trend remains a buyer. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began investigating buyers of more than $10,000 per month, despite the limit imposed by Communication "A" 6770, and the "schools", as the people who are hired to buy the authorized quota with funds outside the legal circuit.\par \par \uc2 The Government was awakened by an unbridled love for controls as if they were solving some of the economics' underlying problems. The largest example is in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, where it limited and set a check and began to refer to the price of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the settlement cash square.\par \par \uc2 This resurgence of new exchange rates had an adverse effect at first because it led to these new dollars trading at about $70. But when the market put together the mechanics to make \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  more fluid, it backed down because they started to make passes between the different dollars. In fact, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered that were sold at the price of the dollar with liquidation - the highest value - to buy the MEP dollar, the stock exchange which is $3 cheaper.\par \par \uc2 From the control of changes the market began to reference the price of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the cash square with liquidation\par \par \uc2 This explains why fixed terms are stabilized, which equates to a monthly loss of 5% in volume because they do not grow at the rate of interest rate. For a week now, they've been parked at 1.5 billion pesos.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the dollar deposits are continuing. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported that last Monday they left the system FOR USD 91 million, a low figure compared to the little more than $300 million that left on Thursday. Dollar outflows have an on-constant drop in reserves. This time $82 million was lost and $49,228 million was left.\par \par \uc2 The dollar in the wholesale plaza with scarce businesses for $312 million rose 14 cents to $57.21 but with the help of official banks because it was eager to close at higher levels. In banks and exchanges, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grew 17 cents to $59.51 and here I need more effort from the official banks because otherwise I could have gotten to about $60. The blue remained at $61.75. At the time the count of liquidity rose to $64.10, while the stock exchange or MEP dollar dropped to 61.53 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Country Risk Index increased to 2,234 basis points (15 units) for \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Bond uprising and 2020 Treasury drop (3.66%) and Bonar 2024, the debt reference title, which lost 0.54 per cent.\par \par \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 's announcements that if he is president he will seek to get Argentina out of this situation of suffocation of the default debt, applying Uruguay's recipe in 2003, i.e. respecting the amount and fees, but lengthening the deadlines, did not change the mood of the markets.\par \par \uc2 Uruguay's plan was 98% accepted by creditors. It was made with a sacrifice that Argentines hardly accept: there was a 10% tax on all salaries in the public sector which allowed it to lower public spending and increase tax collection for the income of private sector workers. In addition, theexchange rate doubled against the dollar to cut the exchange rate.Those who mishandle mathematics speak of the process as the Uruguayan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devalued 100%. The $5.236 million debt stretched its five-year terms, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Uruguay\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not accept the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that asked it to make a set-up. The \uc2 IMF\uc2 's role was occupied by the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2 , which lent $1.5 billion to pay the smaller savers and show support to the largest creditors.\par \par \uc2 The $5.236 million debt stretched its five-year terms, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Uruguay\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not accept the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that asked it to make a set-up. The \uc2 IMF\uc2 's role was held by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\par \par \uc2 The Argentinian case is very different\par \par \uc2 Does anyone think a similar situation will be possible for Argentina? The Government did not even listen to Roberto Lavagna or Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Redrado, who advised him to buy back with $5 billion that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  allowed the 2020 Bonar and other securities that were at settlement prices.\par \par \uc2 Redrado had already done that experience and was successful, in the previous government with the Bonar 2015 who had a parity of 48%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed him to lower the country irrigation. Today in the case of bonar 2020, it would have made it easier for the country to renew the rest of the debt that was due this year without altering the terms of payment and kicking the ghost of the default forward.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Government continues to maintain its monetary policy despite the failure to fight inflation and exchange rate. In the Liquidity Letters (Leliq) tender, he placed $212,543 million with a significant drop in rates from 0.83 points to 79.99% per year. It punctured the floor 80% a year, although it is only a color data because it is still exaggeratedly high. The catch does not cover the maturities and released $4 billion for Friday.\par \par \uc2 !function(e,t,s,i)'var n'"InfogramEmbeds",o'e.getElementsByTagName("script")[0],d'/'http:/.test(e.location)?" http:":"https:";if(/-/-2-/.test(i)&(i-d+i),window[n]&window[n].initialized)window[n].process&window[n].process.process(n].process(process));else if(!e.getElementById(s))-var r-e.createElement("script");r.async-1,r.id-s,r.src-i,o.parentNode.insertBefore(r, o)(document,0,"infogram-async","{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://e.infogram.com/js/dist/embed-loader-min.js"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://e.infogram.com/js/dist/embed-loader-min.js}}}\uc2 ");\par \par \uc2 The Stock Exchange, meanwhile, confirmed that the previous day's rise was the "dead cat bounce" and went down again. While the fall of the S&P Merval, the leading stock index, was slight, just 0.16%, businesses remained low and regularly at around $600 million. The most notable stock was \uc2 Ternium\uc2  with 3.41%. This Techint stock is equivalent to having dollars abroad because the company is based in Texas and engaged in oil. \uc2 Banco Supervielle\uc2  with an increase of 3% had a second positive wheel, just like cement company HARG \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Holcim\uc2 , won 2.38 percent.\par \par \uc2 In Wall Street, Argentine ADRs - stock-holding certificates - had a neutral day where ups and downs were mixed. IRSA Commercial Properties that the previous day had increased by more than 25% this time withstood a profit takeand and lost 8.36%. The most notable rise was that of the Cement company \uc2 Loma Negra\uc2  with 3.86 percent.\par \par \uc2 The business climate remains negative. Elections are a major obstacle because it detracts from the government's power and makes the measures it takes not to generate confidence. In fact, most of the ills suffered by the economy, increased country risk, dollar deposits, low bonds, inflation rises and dollarization of portfolios, are situations born from this environment of power weakness.\par \par \uc2 FollowedReading:Cristiano Rattazzi, about \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2 : "How can there be 30% of Argentines who vote ali Baba and the forty thieves without caring about anything?"\par \par \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  sought to seduce the Red Circle with criticism of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's debt, but also to the strain of \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\par \par \uc2 Economic activity rose in July 0.6%, but was not sustained after the devaluation in August\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190927ef9r001fn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
