\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Moody's\uc2  doubts that Argentina crisis contagion to Latin America\b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 It is unlikely that the turmoil in Argentina's financial markets will spread to the rest of Latin America, except possibly Uruguay, an analyst at rating agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said on Tuesday. A weak economic context, the nervousness with respect to the devaluation and the preoccupation by the crop of soybean hit by the drought in Argentina are pressing to the Argentine peso, that this week fell to a historical minimum against the dollar. Lee: Argentine President faces judicial process of course money laundering. "It is difficult to see a contagion of Argentina's agitation in Latin America," said Mauro Leos, head of sovereign risk at the agency for Latin America and the Caribbean at a conference in London, adding the possible exception in \b \highlight22\uc2 Uruguay\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Lee: The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina performs a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2  The country is facing a crisis and on Tuesday the sovereign bonds in the over-the-counter market of Argentina fall 0.9% on average, in times of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tension in the domestic market and a rapprochement of the Government to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to negotiate a line of credit. The declining trend in government securities was led by dollar-denominated issues, operators said.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180515ee5f003jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
