\par\par \b \uc2  MOODY'S LOWERS FOREIGN  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY \highlight\uc2  DEPOSIT AND DEBT RATINGS OF BANCO COMERCIAL S.A. AND BANCO DE MONTEVIDEO S.A. \b0\par\par\uc2 889 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2002\par \uc2 Moody's Investor Service Press Release\par \uc2 MOODPR\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002\par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service downgraded to Ca from Caa1 the long term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ratings of both Banco Comercial S.A. (Comercial) and Banco de Montevideo S.A. (Montevideo), Uruguay's two largest domestically owned private sector banks. \par \par \uc2  Moody's lowered the long term deposit, and senior and subordinated debt ratings of Comercial and the long term deposit and senior debt ratings of Montevideo in light of indications by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Uruguay that it would only cover the demand deposit and savings account obligations of those privately-owned banks whose \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been suspended. The implication is that the long term fixed rate deposits in US dollars held at those banks as well as their debt obligations would therefore be subject to the banks' own ability to meet those obligations. \par \par \uc2  Moody's indicated that the Ca ratings reflect its expectation of a high severity of loss related to these instruments in light of both banks' fragile financial condition, as well as the low level of support assumed to be forthcoming from their private shareholders as well as from the Uruguayan authorities. \par \par \uc2  Comercial's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were suspended for 30 days by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Uruguay on August 5, 2002, the same day it lifted the bank holiday it had imposed on July 30th for the whole financial system. Comercial had been partially \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased a stake in the bank following a scandal involving its Argentine shareholders. It remains unclear whether Comercial's private shareholders will step in to cover all of the bank's fixed term deposit and debt obligations. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  Montevideo had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 21, 2002 by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Uruguay\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspended the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 30th and has indicated it might liquidate the bank. \par \par \uc2  The following ratings were affected: \par \par \uc2  Banco de Montevideo S.A.: \par \par \uc2  - Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits downgraded to Ca from Caa1. \par \par \uc2  - Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  senior debt downgraded to Ca from Caa1. \par \par \uc2  Banco Comercial S.A.: \par \par \uc2  - Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits downgraded to Ca from Caa1. \par \par \uc2  - Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  senior unsecured debt downgraded to Ca from Caa1. \par \par \uc2  - Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  subordinated debt downgraded to Ca from Caa1. \par \par \uc2  ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED HEREIN IS COPYRIGHTED IN THE NAME OF MOODY'S INVESTORS SERVICE, INC. ("MOODY'S"), AND NONE OF SUCH INFORMATION MAY BE COPIED OR OTHERWISE REPRODUCED, REPACKAGED, FURTHER TRANSMITTED, TRANSFERRED, DISSEMINATED, REDISTRIBUTED OR RESOLD, OR STORED FOR SUBSEQUENT USE FOR ANY SUCH PURPOSE, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, IN ANY FORM OR MANNER OR BY ANY MEANS WHATSOEVER, BY ANY PERSON WITHOUT MOODY'S PRIOR WRITTEN CONSENT. All information contained herein is obtained by 