\par\par \b \uc2  Moody's Lowers Banco Comercial Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  To Ca \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2002\par 20:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones Corporate Filings Alert \par \uc2 FF\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Following is a press release from Moody's Investors Service:\par   New York, August 15, 2002 -- Moody's Investors Service downgraded to Ca\par from Caa1 the long term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ratings of both Banco Comercial S.A.\par (Comercial) and Banco de Montevideo S.A. (Montevideo), Uruguay's two largest\par domestically owned private sector banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Moody's lowered the long term deposit, and senior and subordinated debt\par ratings of Comercial and the long term deposit and senior debt ratings of\par Montevideo in light of indications by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Uruguay that it\par would only cover the demand deposit and savings account obligations of those\par privately-owned banks whose \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been suspended. The implication\par is that the long term fixed rate deposits in US dollars held at those banks\par as well as their debt obligations would therefore be subject to the banks'\par own ability to meet those obligations.\par   Moody's indicated that the Ca ratings reflect its expectation of a high\par severity of loss related to these instruments in light of both banks' fragile\par financial condition, as well as the low level of support assumed to be\par forthcoming from their private shareholders as well as from the Uruguayan\par authorities.\par   Comercial's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were suspended for 30 days by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par Uruguay on August 5, 2002, the same day it lifted the bank holiday it had\par imposed on July 30th for the whole financial system. Comercial had been\par partially \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in February as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchased a stake in the\par bank following a scandal involving its Argentine shareholders. It remains\par unclear whether Comercial's private shareholders will step in to cover all of\par the bank's fixed term deposit and debt obligations.\par   Montevideo had been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on June 21, 2002 by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Uruguay\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspended the bank's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on July 30th and\par has indicated it might liquidate the bank.\par   The following ratings were affected:\par   Banco de Montevideo S.A.:\par   -- Long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deposits downgraded to Ca from Caa1.\par   -- Long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  senior debt downgraded to Ca from Caa1.\par   Banco Comercial S.A.:\par   -- Long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deposits downgraded to Ca from Caa1.\par   -- Long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  senior unsecured debt downgraded to Ca from\par Caa1.\par -- Long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  subordinated debt downgraded to Ca from Caa1.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14:46\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument ff00000020020815dy8f007kb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich4