\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Uruguay floats  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  hit by Argentine problems. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anahi Rama \par \uc2 820 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2002\par 21:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MONTEVIDEO, Uruguay, June 20 (Reuters) - Uruguay floated its peso on Thursday, abruptly ending a decade-old \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band system, as economic chaos spread from neighboring Argentina and market instability from neighboring Brazil. \par \par \uc2  Uruguay's peso RPNJ) slid 18.2 percent to 21 per U.S. dollar at the Thursday mid-session. \par \par \uc2  Uruguay, battered by a deepening recession and banking troubles, is seen by many investors as the front line in the wider battle of Latin American nations fighting to avoid contagion from growing troubles in regional powerhouses Brazil and Argentina. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rates of our two neighbors are heaping major uncertainty on us," Economy Minister Alberto Bension said. \par \par \uc2  Uruguay's international reserves have plummeted over 40 percent this year amid attempts to keep the peso trading within its former band. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there would be only limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the new floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund, which has given financial aid to Uruguay in an effort to keep it from spiraling down with Argentina, said Uruguay was a "classic contagion case" and welcomed the nation's "bold" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move, while the U.S. Treasury praised the float as a "strengthened" \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  The IMF may increase aid by $1.5 billion on top of a $769 million loan approved in March. \par \par \uc2  But any dramatic fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries investors, who fear it could hurt the country's ability to service its $3 billion foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  Uruguay - dependent on banking, tourism and agriculture and on Argentina's own recession-hit economy - has been battered by a run on banks and a dive in consumer spending, which saw GDP drop 10 percent in the first quarter. That forced a country once dubbed the "Switzerland of South America" to seek IMF aid. \par \par \uc2  Exasperated Uruguayan President Jorge Batlle this month slammed Argentine politicians as a "band of thieves" when asked about Argentina's impact on his economy. He later blamed the outburst on the stress of dealing with his country's crisis. \par \par \uc2  "We're going to end up like Argentina," said Roberto Muniz, a security guard in the capital. In this country of 3 million people that is double the size of Portugal, 15 percent of the work force is unemployed. \par \par \uc2  The free float decision comes six months after Argentina, Latin America's third-largest economy, devalued its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by cutting it loose from a rigid one-to-one exchange rate with the U.S. dollar amid an economic crisis. The move sent shock waves across the River Plate to Uruguay. \par \par \uc2  "They want to obviously try to preserve their international reserves and not spend them on the defense of some arbitrary exchange rate band. So from that perspective, the decision will help them do that," said Marco Santamaria, sovereign strategist at Lehman Brothers in New York. \par \par \uc2  "(But) if the exchange rate were to depreciate substantively, Uruguay's debt burden would become more difficult to manage in peso terms," he added. \par \par \uc2  Troubles in Brazil, fueled by investor worries that turbulence ahead of October's presidential elections will make it difficult to manage the country's hefty $274 billion debt load, have also hit Uruguay. \par \par \uc2  URUGUAY FOLLOWS ARGENTINA \par \par \uc2  Argentina's peso has fallen by over 70 percent against the dollar since January, sparking escalating inflation and putting basic food and goods out of the reach of millions of increasingly poor Argentines. \par \par \uc2  Under \b \highlight22\uc2 Uruguay\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band system, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading within a certain range. Uruguay's previous system of controlled devaluations had left its exports unable to keep pace with those of major trading partner Argentina amid its steep peso fall. \par \par \uc2  "It's an important move," one emerging market debt trader said of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float. "The IMF probably asked them to do it as part of the package they gave them." \par \par \uc2  As well as the new IMF loan, Uruguay has recently also won $500 million in aid from the Inter-American Bank, and the World Bank has pledged to lend $400 million over two years. \par \par \uc2  Uruguay's sovereign bonds did not react immediately to the news. \par \par \uc2  Bond prices had plummeted as investors shied away from Uruguayan debt while the country has been paralyzed by strikes against tax hikes and austerity measures. \par \par \uc2  Uruguay's problems have been compounded by a string of downgrades from ratings agencies, which expressed concern that Argentina's financial mess had sent Uruguay's bank deposits and reserves tumbling. \par \par \uc2  When ratings agencies lower credit ratings it becomes more expensive to sell bonds, undermining a government's ability to fund its budget. \par \par \uc2  Argentina has been embroiled in a massive economic crisis since the IMF cut off access to a $22 billion loan in December, an action quickly followed by default on part of its $140 billion debt and the disastrous devaluation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020620dy6k0116x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
