o help Banco Galicia \b \highlight22\uc2 Uruguay\b0 \highlight\uc2  SA in February after it lost about $500 million in December and January - roughly a third of total deposits - after a run on deposits at the Argentine parent bank sent depositors clamoring to withdraw funds from the Uruguayan institution. \par \par \uc2  The original plan meant a $43 million cash injection, matching the amount of term deposits held by depositors in Banco Galicia Uruguay, a bank spokesman said in Montevideo. \par \par \uc2  Last month, three major credit rating agencies downgraded the ratings of many Uruguayan banks with negative outlooks to reflect the government's own downgrade, resulting from dropping \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and the decline of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020618dy6i011yr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
